{
  "_comment": "fetch_many(urls, options): the JSON body sent to POST /v1/fetch (\"body\" cases) and what a success body becomes (\"responses\" cases). Options mirror the request groups: content {max_chars, objective, links, images}, retrieval {max_age_hours, as_of}, plus deadline_ms and session_id; each SDK maps the names to its own spelling (Python keeps them, TypeScript uses camelCase, Go and Rust use struct fields). Body rules: urls are sent as given (a lone string is wrapped in a list). A group is sent when it is given, holding only the fields set; an empty string means unset, and there are no sentinel values: max_chars 0 (metadata only) and max_age_hours 0 (always live) are sent. max_age_hours is a number, fractions allowed. Fields the API rejects together (max_age_hours with as_of) are sent for the API to reject. deadline_ms and session_id are sent as given. `sent` is the whole body, compared as JSON. Response rules: results, notices and warnings are lists of objects (anything else is []), non-object entries skipped. request_id is the body's non-blank string, else the trimmed X-Request-Id header, else null. status is a string or null. summary has integer requested, succeeded and failed (0 otherwise). resolved keeps the string values of an object ({} otherwise). A result's index is an integer from 0 (else its position in the list); requested_url, url and status are strings (\"\" otherwise); title, published_at, acquired_at, image, favicon and retrieved_from a non-blank string or null. Its content (from the content object, {} otherwise): text a string or null; total_chars an integer from 0 or null; links [{url, text}] and images [{url, alt}] (url \"\" and text/alt null for anything else), or null when not a list. error is null unless it is an object; then type, code, message are strings (\"\" otherwise), fix a string or null, retryable a boolean (false otherwise), upstream_status details.upstream_status as an integer or null. A notice or warning has code and message strings (\"\" otherwise) and path a string or null (details kept raw, not compared). usage is the object as sent, or null, and is not compared; neither are details on notices, warnings and errors. latency_ms an integer from 0 or null; session_id a non-blank string or null. `skip` names an SDK whose types cannot express the case, with why.",
